The skill told the agent to send revisions with -v N but said nothing
about the interdiff, which is why revised series kept going out
without one. It now asks for --interdiff and shows where to find the
previous version's head: git format-patch names each patch's
Message-ID after its commit, so the head of the last version is the
hash leading the Message-ID of its last patch. The mail workflow
guide states the same rule.
