-cover letter blurb with what changed and a link to the previous
-version:
+**Revisions.** For a revised series add `-v N` and
+`--interdiff=<head of v(N-1)>`. format-patch.sh refuses a reroll
+without an interdiff, which shows the reviewer exactly what changed
+since the version they read; git puts it in the cover letter, or below
+the `---` of a single patch. git names each patch's Message-ID after
+its commit, so the previous head is the leading hash of the last
+patch's Message-ID in v(N-1):
+
+    prev="<Message-ID of the last patch of v(N-1)>"
+    prev_head="${prev%%.*}"
+    git cat-file -e "${prev_head}^{commit}"
+
+If trunk moved between versions, the interdiff shows trunk's changes
+too; say so in the version notes.
+
+Address every review point the list researcher found unaddressed, or
+say why not. End the cover letter blurb with what changed and a link
+to the previous version:
 
     Changes in vN:
     - <what changed, and why>
